From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 21:00:00 +0000
Subject: drm/sun4i: de33 writeback: Capture only the job's own snapshot

A job that could not start at the vblank that wrote its commit out was
started later on whatever was on screen then: the "picture unchanged"
check compared against the snapshot seen when the job first reached
the head of an idle unit, not against the job's own snapshot. Under a
4K decode plus a memcpy load the unit was still writing out the
previous capture at that vblank (de33_wb_busy_frames), the job started
one frame late and recorded the next commit's picture as its own, with
a good fence (two "early" captures in 600 flips; the scan-out itself
was right, every flip event and flush one vblank apart). A commit
coalesced with the next one before a flush had the same effect.

Compare with the job's own latch_seq instead, and fail such a job with
-EIO (de33_wb_lost) as a picture replaced after an OVERFLOW already
was. Look at the following jobs in the same interrupt, so the next
job, whose snapshot is the one on screen, still starts at once.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun50i_wb.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun50i_wb.c
@@ -200,13 +200,6 @@
 	/* the mixer snapshot holding this job's commit (sun50i_wb_arm()) */
 	bool			armed;
 	unsigned int		latch_seq;
-	/*
-	 * The snapshot on screen when the job could first start: a capture
-	 * postponed or repeated later records the same picture only while
-	 * no other snapshot has been written out since.
-	 */
-	bool			eligible;
-	unsigned int		frame_seq;
 	unsigned int		tries;		/* captures started */
 	unsigned int		deferred;	/* starts postponed */
 	int			status;
@@ -606,39 +599,43 @@
 		}
 	}
 
-	if (!wb->running && !list_empty(&wb->pending)) {
+	/*
+	 * A job starts at the vblank of its own CRTC, once the latch flush
+	 * wrote its commit's registers: started earlier it would capture the
+	 * previous frame. It captures its own picture only while snapshot
+	 * latch_seq is the one on screen: a job that could not start at that
+	 * vblank (the unit still writing out the previous capture, a start
+	 * postponed, a repeat after OVERFLOW) or whose commit was coalesced
+	 * with the next one would record a later commit's picture as its
+	 * own. Such a job fails, and the next one is looked at.
+	 */
+	while (!wb->running && !list_empty(&wb->pending)) {
 		job = list_first_entry(&wb->pending, struct sun50i_wb_job,
 				       list);
-		/*
-		 * A job starts at the vblank of its own CRTC, once the latch
-		 * flush wrote its commit's registers: started earlier it would
-		 * capture the previous frame.
-		 */
-		if (job->mixer == mixer && job->armed &&
-		    (int)(flushed - job->latch_seq) >= 0) {
-			if (!job->eligible) {
-				job->eligible = true;
-				job->frame_seq = flushed;
-			}
+		if (job->mixer != mixer || !job->armed ||
+		    (int)(flushed - job->latch_seq) < 0)
+			break;
+
+		if (flushed != job->latch_seq) {
+			/* the job's picture is no longer on screen */
+			list_del(&job->list);
+			de33_wb_lost++;
+			sun50i_wb_job_end(&done, job, -EIO);
+			continue;
+		}
 
-			if (flushed != job->frame_seq) {
-				/* the job's picture is no longer on screen */
-				list_del(&job->list);
-				de33_wb_lost++;
-				sun50i_wb_job_end(&done, job, -EIO);
-			} else if (late &&
-				   job->deferred < SUN50I_WB_MAX_BUSY_FRAMES) {
-				job->deferred++;
-				de33_wb_deferred++;
-			} else {
-				list_del(&job->list);
-				wb->running = job;
-				job->tries++;
-				if ((int)cur_line > de33_wb_start_line_max)
-					de33_wb_start_line_max = cur_line;
-				sun50i_wb_start(wb, job);
-			}
+		if (late && job->deferred < SUN50I_WB_MAX_BUSY_FRAMES) {
+			job->deferred++;
+			de33_wb_deferred++;
+			break;
 		}
+
+		list_del(&job->list);
+		wb->running = job;
+		job->tries++;
+		if ((int)cur_line > de33_wb_start_line_max)
+			de33_wb_start_line_max = cur_line;
+		sun50i_wb_start(wb, job);
 	}
 
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&wb->lock, flags);
